  "examples": {
    "q01": {
      "question": "When a release is rolled back, how does the script figure out which revision should get the traffic again?",
      "answer": "Roll back to stable; `./scripts/rollback.sh` (revision with the most traffic) or `./scripts/rollback.sh <revision>`; no [4] `rollback.sh` used to pin 100% of traffic to a hard-coded revision. [2] `canary.sh` puts it at 20% next to the revision that currently has the most traffic, then a person decides: `promote.sh` (100%) or `rollback.sh` (back to stable). [1]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/runbook.md#1",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/runbook.md#4",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/architecture.md#4"
      ]
    },
    "q02": {
      "question": "Why can't the promotion decision in the training pipeline reuse a result from an earlier run?",
      "answer": "`pipelines/risk_train_pipeline.py` (KFP v2 on Vertex AI Pipelines): `features-bq` \u2192 `train-xgboost` \u2192 `evaluate-gold` \u2192 `dsl.If` promote \u2192 `register-model`, `dsl.Else` \u2192 `notify-rejected`. [2] Never submit while a `risk-train-eval` run is queued or running. [4] *\"Why is caching disabled on the gate?\"* With caching, a re-run with the same inputs would reuse the old decision even though the champion changed. [1]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#5",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#12",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#6"
      ]
    },
    "q03": {
      "question": "Why is the risk model served from Cloud Run rather than from a managed Vertex AI prediction endpoint?",
      "answer": "Cloud Run instead of a Vertex AI Endpoint for serving. [1] `min-instances=0` on Cloud Run, Cloud Run Jobs instead of always-on services, no Vertex AI Endpoints (Cloud Run serves the model), CPU-only pipeline components. [2] A risk classifier retrains itself: features in BigQuery, a Vertex AI pipeline that only promotes a model if it beats the current one on a gold set, Model Registry, canary releases on Cloud Run with instant rollback, and a daily drift job that retrains when the inputs move. [4]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/architecture.md#8",
        "invoice-mlops/infra/README.md#3",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#22"
      ]
    },
    "q04": {
      "question": "Why do the Gemini calls go to the EU multi-region instead of the region where the rest of the project is deployed?",
      "answer": "The `eu` multi-region keeps processing in the EU. [1] Checked on 2026-10-22 on the Vertex AI generative AI pricing page, Gemini 3.8 Flash, `eu` multi-region (\"non-global\") rate: [2] The default model is `gemini-3.8-flash` on the `eu` endpoint, because no GA Flash model was served from `europe-west4` regionally on 2026-10-22. [3]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/architecture.md#8",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/cost.md#3",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#15"
      ]
    },
    "q05": {
      "question": "Why does the risk classifier look so much worse on its holdout split than on the curated gold set?",
      "answer": "*\"Why is holdout F1 (0.67) so far below gold F1 (0.86)?\"* The holdout labels carry the 8% noise, so even a perfect learner of the policy is penalised there. [2] Small data: on 120 gold invoices, one wrong prediction moves F1 by about 0.01. [4] gold set `data/gold/risk_gold.csv`; 120; clean (no flips), different seed; 0.863; 0.957; 0.786 [1]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#2",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/model_card.md#1",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/model_card.md#0"
      ]
    },
    "q06": {
      "question": "Why doesn't the API write the prediction log in a background task after it has already responded?",
      "answer": "*\"Why is logging synchronous?\"* Cloud Run may throttle CPU after the response is sent, so background tasks are not reliable without \"CPU always allocated\". [2] *\"Logging failed, what does the client see?\"* A normal answer. [1]",
      "cited": [
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#8",
        "invoice-mlops/docs/walkthrough.md#9"
      ]
    }
  },
